IMPORT daydate

-- Superannuation Industry (Supervision) Act 1993 (Cth), insurance-in-super encoding: the date arithmetic, kept in one
-- small module so that daydate is imported in one place only. See NOTES.md.

-- The same day of the month N months later; a day the later month lacks becomes its last day (29 February + 72 months
-- is 28 February).
GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE, `n` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the day N months after` MEANS
    `add months` `the day` `n`

-- Whether the first day falls on or before the second.
GIVEN `first` IS A DATE, `second` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`is on or before` MEANS
    DATE_SERIAL `first` AT MOST DATE_SERIAL `second`

-- Whether the first day falls before the second.
GIVEN `first` IS A DATE, `second` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`is before` MEANS
    DATE_SERIAL `first` LESS THAN DATE_SERIAL `second`

-- A date from day, month and year, for the other modules and the case file (which do not import daydate themselves).
GIVEN `d` IS A NUMBER, `m` IS A NUMBER, `y` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the date` MEANS
    Date `d` `m` `y`
